WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:05.805
-I had a joke
where the punchline was

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.340
"Ibiza."

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.874
Didn't land.

00:00:08.874 --> 00:00:10.710
Then I opined,
maybe it didn't land

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.612
because I didn't say
"I-bith-a."

00:00:13.612 --> 00:00:15.314
Many of you said
the bigger problem

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:18.985
was the way I said
"Ibiza" made it sound like

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:21.054
I said "a pizza."

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.393
Someone wrote, "The worst thing
about watching 'Corrections'

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:29.963
in an area
with bad internet connectivity

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:31.531
is I can't always
immediately tell

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:33.399
when the video is buffering

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:36.803
or if Seth is holding for the
laughs that will never come."

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:44.177
Hurtful.

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:47.647
I hope broadband
never comes to where you live.

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:58.124
Well, it happened. The crew has
started a "Corrections" pool.

00:01:01.093 --> 00:01:04.530
There is now a weekly
"Corrections" picture,

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:08.934
a series of boxes
like a Super Bowl pool,

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:10.436
and everyone picks a box.

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:12.905
And then after all
the boxes have names,

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:15.141
they randomly assign
the numbers.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:19.779
There's a minutes column
and a seconds column.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:23.316
So if corrections
ends up at 17:13,

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:26.553
it would be a seven,
and three would be the payoff.

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:28.621
Our associate director,
Amy Mancini,

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.490
does the official time.

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:39.265
And here's how it's changed
"Corrections" for me.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:45.939
The second it ends,

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:51.210
I watch Kenny Coyle
poring over the boxes

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.446
like a guy who owns his bookie

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:57.283
$1 million.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.851
Just ripping it up,
being like,

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:01.788
"[Bleep] Animal Flubs
[bleep] me!

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:07.694
I was right on time
and then the [bleep] Flubs."

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:17.003
Paul won last week.

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:20.373
Paul is the cameraman
who stands next to Buck,

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:24.510
and he used his winnings
on the most beautiful

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.813
noise-canceling headphones.

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:34.954
Headphones I assumed
he was already wearing

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:41.928
based on the lack of laughs
I was getting from ol' Paul.

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:49.869
We talked about the lack of
elevated debate in Congress

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.370
and how people
are talking in a way

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.205
they didn't used
to talk before,

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:57.677
and I compared it
to the Lincoln-Douglas debates,

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:59.412
and someone said, "Bad choice.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:02.714
Racial slurs were used
in the Lincoln-Douglas debates."

00:03:02.714 --> 00:03:04.918
Let me guess, Douglas?

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:13.493
I was very proud of my
oubliette joke last week.

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:15.194
Many of you asked if my mom,

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:17.496
a former middle school
French teacher,

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:20.966
had enjoyed it
and I did give her a heads up.

00:03:20.966 --> 00:03:23.836
I said, "When you
watch 'Corrections' this week,

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:26.906
there's a joke
I put in just for you."

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:28.474
And then yesterday,

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.244
I called home
and I was talking to my mom

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:33.679
and I said, "Did you like
the oubliette joke?"

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:36.582
And she said,
"I don't think I saw it yet."

00:03:36.582 --> 00:03:39.318
And then my dad
from the background, said,

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:41.353
"We saw it yesterday."

00:03:41.353 --> 00:03:44.390
And then she said,
"Oh, yeah. It was great."

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:53.433
Literally a day later,
and she already oubli-ate.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:05.444 line:0%
We had a joke about a teenager
TP-ing my house

00:04:05.444 --> 00:04:08.648 line:0%
and someone said,
"That's not a teenager."

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:13.185
They also then pointed out

00:04:13.185 --> 00:04:16.189
he wasn't a teenager
last week either...

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:24.096
...when he was working
at a carnival.

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:27.900
And this is the burn

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.569
when you're
the 12:30 show on NBC.

00:04:30.569 --> 00:04:33.739
They won't --
not only will they not license

00:04:33.739 --> 00:04:37.643
a photo of a real-looking
teenager for us,

00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:40.947
we got to use the 27-year-old
more than once.

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:48.087
Meanwhile, they shut down
Fifth Avenue

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:51.724
so that Jimmy
could do a pre-tape with BTS.

00:04:59.164 --> 00:05:00.833
"You can't give me a picture
of a 14-year-old?"

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:02.468
"We can't do it."

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:11.344
As someone else has said,
I think we have used Devin.

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:15.480
Devin is the name of our
28-year-old teenager.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:16.916
We've used him before,

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:18.484
so we're going to go back
through the archives

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:20.486
and see how many times
we've used him.

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:23.789
Oh, we talked about --
Sal wrote about how

00:05:23.789 --> 00:05:27.593
the Ohio GOP was trying to
overturn the voters' decision

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:30.663
in regards to a woman's
right to an abortion,

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:33.865
and he cited Marbury v. Madison.

00:05:33.865 --> 00:05:35.768
And then someone said,
"That actually wouldn't apply.

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:39.071
That is only a federal ruling,

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:42.774
so that would not apply
to a state ruling in Ohio."

00:05:42.774 --> 00:05:45.178
Which just proves what I've been
saying for a long time,

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:46.813
which is, Sal's dumb as [bleep].

00:05:56.088 --> 00:05:58.224
You said Scooby-Doo
couldn't pull the mask off

00:05:58.224 --> 00:06:00.025
because he lacks
opposable thumbs.

00:06:00.025 --> 00:06:03.329
That is a very fair point.

00:06:05.364 --> 00:06:10.403
I think we all watch that show
for its sense of accuracy.

00:06:10.403 --> 00:06:13.606
Because dogs, of course,
can have a very acute

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:15.708
sense of danger,

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:20.880
and when a dog senses danger,
it will often say, "Ruh-roh."

00:06:24.683 --> 00:06:27.586
I was told my Shaggy --
and again, I had some bad --

00:06:27.586 --> 00:06:30.456
I had some janky impressions
this week.

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:32.358
I had a cold.

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:38.397
I saw my Shaggy sounded like
Werner Herzog,

00:06:38.397 --> 00:06:40.599
which it does not,

00:06:40.599 --> 00:06:42.502
but I wish it did.

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:47.039
[ As Werner Herzog ]
"Once again, Scooby...

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:53.812
...we find ourselves in
an unfortunate situation.

00:06:53.812 --> 00:07:01.387
Hearts full of terror,
bellies empty of a pizza pie.

00:07:08.293 --> 00:07:11.663
Our terror makes us run,

00:07:11.663 --> 00:07:13.599
our feet moving
as fast as we can,

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:17.903
and yet we stay in one place

00:07:17.903 --> 00:07:22.174
as they fail to find purchase.

00:07:22.174 --> 00:07:24.710
In times like this, Scoobs...

00:07:26.845 --> 00:07:31.083
...that one can only turn
to a solitary word --

00:07:32.918 --> 00:07:34.720
zoinks!"

00:07:40.392 --> 00:07:44.463
-Oh, we made a joke
about Don Jr.

00:07:44.463 --> 00:07:46.098
looking like he was about
to get a colonoscopy.

00:07:46.098 --> 00:07:47.433
Someone said, "You know,
that's very funny,

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:50.202
but you should use your platform
to stress the importance

00:07:50.202 --> 00:07:51.370
of getting a colonoscopy."

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.973
So...

00:07:53.973 --> 00:07:57.076
if you were on the fence...

00:08:00.346 --> 00:08:02.481
...and needed to
hear that from me

00:08:02.481 --> 00:08:06.619
in the body of "Corrections,"

00:08:06.619 --> 00:08:08.521
maybe get everything
checked out.

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:19.298
Don Jr. said his dad could
see things other people can't.

00:08:19.298 --> 00:08:22.000
Our joke was, "Like three ghosts
every Christmas Eve."

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:25.837
Many of you said that Scrooge
was actually visited

00:08:25.837 --> 00:08:30.676
by four spirits,
counting Jacob Marley and...

00:08:30.676 --> 00:08:32.144
The joke, I will say, three --

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:36.048
The joke just worked better
with three.

00:08:36.048 --> 00:08:39.685
You know, because the book
has the famous line,

00:08:39.685 --> 00:08:41.487
"You will be haunted
by three spirits."

00:08:41.487 --> 00:08:44.023
So I think that's why
we did the joke that way.

00:08:44.023 --> 00:08:46.325
But I will say, jackals
were a huge problem

00:08:46.325 --> 00:08:48.994
for Dickens as well.

00:08:48.994 --> 00:08:53.298
And there were two
versions of each of his books.

00:08:53.298 --> 00:08:56.468
Like this is "A Christmas Carol:
Jack Addiction."

00:08:56.468 --> 00:08:57.770 line:0%
"Jack Edition," excuse me.

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:01.940 line:0%
Either Jacks is what --

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:05.878 line:0%
jackals were called
Jacks in 1850s England.

00:09:05.878 --> 00:09:07.914 line:0%
Or more likely, I didn't --

00:09:07.914 --> 00:09:10.182 line:0%
I didn't proofread
my email to Ellen.

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:22.361
Definitely picks it up.

00:09:22.361 --> 00:09:25.564
I was like, "No, [bleep], what?

00:09:25.564 --> 00:09:27.233
Well, okay."

00:09:29.535 --> 00:09:32.438
So this is the Jackal Edition...

00:09:34.973 --> 00:09:36.742
...of "A Christmas Carol."

00:09:36.742 --> 00:09:38.778
Because again, it was --
jackals, you know,

00:09:38.778 --> 00:09:40.012
they've existed.

00:09:40.012 --> 00:09:41.847
It didn't just start with me.

00:09:45.217 --> 00:09:47.386
"'That is no light
part of my penance,'

00:09:47.386 --> 00:09:48.420
pursued the ghost.

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:50.422
'I am here tonight to warn you

00:09:50.422 --> 00:09:54.026
that you have yet a chance
and hope of escaping my fate,

00:09:54.026 --> 00:09:57.729
a chance and hope
of my procuring, Ebenezer.'

00:09:57.729 --> 00:10:00.132
'You were always a good
friend to me,' said Scrooge.

00:10:00.132 --> 00:10:01.299
'Thank'ee.

00:10:01.299 --> 00:10:03.468
You will be haunted,'
resumed the ghost,

00:10:03.468 --> 00:10:05.303
'by three spirits.'

00:10:05.303 --> 00:10:08.307
Scrooge's countenance
fell almost as low

00:10:08.307 --> 00:10:10.009
as the ghost's had done.

00:10:10.009 --> 00:10:12.345
'When you say three,'
asked Scrooge,

00:10:12.345 --> 00:10:14.347
'are you counting yourself?'

00:10:17.316 --> 00:10:21.053
Marley paused,
confused by the query.

00:10:21.053 --> 00:10:22.721
'What?' he asked.

00:10:22.721 --> 00:10:25.858
'It's just,' said Scrooge,

00:10:25.858 --> 00:10:29.061
'technically, you're also
a spirit who's haunting me,

00:10:29.061 --> 00:10:33.999
so I just want to know if I
should count you in my three.'

00:10:33.999 --> 00:10:36.735
'I don't count,' said Marley.

00:10:36.735 --> 00:10:38.970
'It's three starting now.'

00:10:38.970 --> 00:10:43.542
'So four total?' asked Scrooge.

00:10:43.542 --> 00:10:45.510
'It doesn't matter,'
said Marley,

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:49.581
getting frustrated by Scrooge's
pedantic attention to detail.

00:10:49.581 --> 00:10:51.416
'It matters to me,'
said Scrooge.

00:10:51.416 --> 00:10:55.253
'Fine, you'll be visited
by three spirits,

00:10:55.253 --> 00:10:57.389
four if you count me,'
said Marley.

00:10:57.389 --> 00:11:01.159
'See?' said Scrooge
with a self-satisfied look.

00:11:01.159 --> 00:11:03.529
'That wasn't so hard.'

00:11:03.529 --> 00:11:05.364
Marley collapsed into a chair

00:11:05.364 --> 00:11:07.900
and considered calling
the whole thing off.

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:09.835
Even if the ghost
did help teach his friend

00:11:09.835 --> 00:11:11.404
the true meaning
of Christmas,

00:11:11.404 --> 00:11:13.338
they were never going to
change the fact

00:11:13.338 --> 00:11:15.908
that he was a [bleep] jackal."

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:23.015
Who do you think Trump's
Jacob Marley would be?

00:11:23.015 --> 00:11:25.050
Roy Cohn, right?

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:27.453
That's who I feel like
who's going to visit him.

00:11:27.453 --> 00:11:29.588
Mine's definitely
going to be Shoemaker.

00:11:33.025 --> 00:11:34.727
He knows it, too.

00:11:34.727 --> 00:11:36.695
Like, sometimes I'll be at
my desk, I'll just look up.

00:11:36.695 --> 00:11:38.297
He'll be in the doorway,
eating an apple,

00:11:38.297 --> 00:11:41.267
being like, "You think
I'm irritating now?"

00:11:45.771 --> 00:11:47.405
"And I'm not bringing
three other ghosts.

00:11:47.405 --> 00:11:49.942
It's just going to be me
in different wigs."

00:11:53.679 --> 00:11:58.217
You dock boats.
You don't park them.

00:12:04.122 --> 00:12:05.724
And I assure you, the writer
who made that mistake

00:12:05.724 --> 00:12:07.093
will be getting his pay parked.

00:12:07.093 --> 00:12:08.761
Our...

00:12:08.761 --> 00:12:11.096
[ Laughter ]

00:12:11.096 --> 00:12:17.168
Hey, our YouTube videos
are not available in Canada.

00:12:17.168 --> 00:12:19.772
And a lot of Canadians --
This is a recent development.

00:12:19.772 --> 00:12:21.273
A lot of Canadians
have been asking,

00:12:21.273 --> 00:12:22.808
"Did we do something
to offend you?"

00:12:22.808 --> 00:12:25.211
Ryan Reynolds.

00:12:25.211 --> 00:12:28.814
I should have been Deadpool.

00:12:28.814 --> 00:12:30.482
We actually don't know
why it happened,

00:12:30.482 --> 00:12:32.351
and we're looking into it.

00:12:32.351 --> 00:12:33.819
We did not do it on purpose.

00:12:33.819 --> 00:12:36.755
It was not a choice we made,

00:12:36.755 --> 00:12:39.759
but we did make sure you could
still enjoy "Corrections."

00:12:45.230 --> 00:12:47.566
I said,
Randy 'Macho Man' Savage."

00:12:47.566 --> 00:12:50.869
I was told it's
"Macho Man Randy Savage."

00:12:50.869 --> 00:12:53.004
I was also told
I have a terrible

00:12:53.004 --> 00:12:54.873
Macho Man Randy Savage
impression.

00:12:54.873 --> 00:12:56.274
Well, joke's on you.

00:12:56.274 --> 00:12:59.111
I was doing
Randy "Macho Man" Savage.

00:13:01.579 --> 00:13:03.382
And that's how he sounds.

00:13:07.586 --> 00:13:10.723
Oh, but his hand can do that?
Okay.

00:13:16.729 --> 00:13:20.865
I did a phone gag last week.

00:13:20.865 --> 00:13:26.004
If you missed it, it will be on
the "Best of Corrections" DVD.

00:13:26.004 --> 00:13:27.873
Someone wrote in and said,

00:13:27.873 --> 00:13:31.509
"Assuming that is a Western
Electric Model 500 telephone,

00:13:31.509 --> 00:13:34.947
which it appears to be,
the ring sound effect played

00:13:34.947 --> 00:13:36.448
is entirely wrong.

00:13:36.448 --> 00:13:39.150
Not only is the Model 500's ring
much higher-pitched,

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:40.519
it's also dual tone."

00:13:40.519 --> 00:13:41.653
So it's official.

00:13:41.653 --> 00:13:45.024
There's [bleep]
phone jackals now.

00:13:47.993 --> 00:13:50.028
A lot of you said the problem
with the joke, too,

00:13:50.028 --> 00:13:51.463
is that I took a call.

00:13:51.463 --> 00:13:54.166
The phone wasn't plugged in.

00:13:54.166 --> 00:13:56.001
This is my cell.

00:13:59.671 --> 00:14:02.908
Oh, sorry.
This isn't my cell phone.

00:14:02.908 --> 00:14:06.779
"Corrections" is a cell
of my own making.

00:14:10.349 --> 00:14:14.053
A prison.

00:14:14.053 --> 00:14:15.720
Hey, we're going to throw --

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:17.456
because some of you
have been asking,

00:14:17.456 --> 00:14:21.025
we're going to
throw the PO box back up.

00:14:21.025 --> 00:14:25.965 line:0%
Don't use it to
send dumb [bleep]

00:14:25.965 --> 00:14:30.636 line:0%
I can show to pad
the length of "Corrections."

00:14:33.638 --> 00:14:36.442 line:0%
That's not what it's for.

00:14:39.278 --> 00:14:40.712
What?

00:14:40.712 --> 00:14:42.881
What do you mean
I have to be done in 15 seconds?

00:14:42.881 --> 00:14:44.183
Not my [bleep] problem, Kenny.

00:14:44.183 --> 00:14:45.551
It's not my [bleep] problem
you're in the hole.

00:14:45.551 --> 00:14:47.018
It's not my [bleep] problem!
That's why --

00:14:47.018 --> 00:14:48.254
Uh, see me next week.

